how every recipe as a numbered summary.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":122,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"b048e176adfee7bcee85eea5afdcd5968b67483f","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add Command hierarchy, Parser, and command stubs","messageBody":"- Command: abstract base with execute(RecipeList, Ui) and isExit().\n- ExitCommand: ends the app on \"bye\" or \"exit\".\n- Parser: splits input into a command word + arguments, and maps the\n  word to a Command via a switch statement.\n- AddCommand/RetrieveCommand/SearchCommand: minimal stubs (constructor\n  + a \"not yet implemented\" execute()) for Persons B/C/D to fill in,\n  already wired into Parser\u0027s switch.\nEach command is its own subclass rather than one class branching on\nthe command word, so implementing add/retrieve/search means editing a\ndedicated file instead of a shared method.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":172,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"95b7d14d4aefdcb9b4fad23750efb81058ddab1a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Wire up the main loop and add skeleton tests","messageBody":"WhatsCooking.main() now runs the real loop: read a line via Ui, parse\nit into a Command via Parser, execute it against a shared RecipeList,\nrepeat until isExit(). Every WhatsCookingException is caught in one\nplace, so a bad command shows an error and the loop continues instead\nof crashing.\nAdds RecipeListTest (bounds-checking) and ParserTest (dispatch to\nExitCommand, rejection of unknown commands) as a template for Persons\nB/C/D\u0027s own command tests.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":26,"deletions":4},"test-code":{"insertions":65,"deletions":0}}}]}],"wunicorn21":[{"date":"2026-09-30T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"aff4d23dfe9cfad86db29aadd4deefe3c4360a56","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"added Lim Sin\u0027s github and name","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":5,"deletions":5}}}